  "lesson": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "More biliterals, building on <a href=\"/egyptology/middle-egyptian-1/biliterals/\">Biliteral Signs</a>. Several of these are pictures of birds and animals that are easy to mix up, so look closely."
      },
      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "More two-consonant signs: the pintail duck <span class=\"eg-h\" style=\"font-size:1.6em;line-height:1\">𓅭</span> <i class=\"eg-tl\">zꜣ</i>, the raised arms <span class=\"eg-h\" style=\"font-size:1.6em;line-height:1\">𓂓</span> <i class=\"eg-tl\">kꜣ</i>, the eye <span class=\"eg-h\" style=\"font-size:1.6em;line-height:1\">𓁹</span> <i class=\"eg-tl\">jr</i>, the fox skins <span class=\"eg-h\" style=\"font-size:1.6em;line-height:1\">𓄟</span> <i class=\"eg-tl\">ms</i>, the club <span class=\"eg-h\" style=\"font-size:1.6em;line-height:1\">𓍛</span> <i class=\"eg-tl\">ḥm</i> and the sickle <span class=\"eg-h\" style=\"font-size:1.6em;line-height:1\">𓌳</span> <i class=\"eg-tl\">mꜣ</i>."
      },
      {
        "t": "table",
